                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A temporal extension of Basic Formal Ontology implemented in the Web Ontology Language (OWL 2) with direct semantics."@en ,
                                                                                   """ClimOO Ontology is a reference ontology, modeling plastics, (micro-)plastic pollution, climate change, and their interrelation, with a primary focus on agricultural systems. The ClimOO Ontology is structured in a suite of nested ontological modules.The SDC2 module forks the Sustainable Development and Climate (SDC) Ontology, updating the proposed models. The SDC2 module centers on climate and climate change, especially with regard to environmental features and related interconnections. Emphasis is also dedicated to relevant policies.

SDC ontology: https://github.com/hbabaie1/Sustainable-Development-and-Climate-SDC-ontology"""@en ,
                                                                                   """SCO V1.1.0 aligns with two Top-Level Ontologies (TLOs), Basic Formal Ontology (BFO) and Unified Foundational Ontology (UFO). SCO V1.1.0 is comprised of two segments: SCO-B (B for BFO) and SCO-U (U for UFO). SCO-B aligns the SCO vocabulary with BFO (as SCO V1.0.0). SCO-U aligns the SCO vocabulary with gUFO (UFO implementation in the Web Ontology Language (OWL)). This file provides SCO-B segment.

References – TLOs:  
https://github.com/BFO-ontology/BFO-2020 
https://ontouml.readthedocs.io/en/latest/intro/ufo.html 
https://nemo-ufes.github.io/gufo/"""@en-au ,
                                                                                   """SCO is a middle-level ontology, representing the major theoretical challenges to sustainability:
1) The polysemy of the term sustainability.
2) The relationship between sustainability and sustainable development.
3) The complexity underlying sustainability.
SCO aims to play a pivotal role in harmonizing and integrating top-level and domain ontologies regarding sustainability."""@en ,
                                                                                   """This file contains ClimOO Ontology imports from the Common Core Ontology suite (CCO). Imports were manually collected and revised.

Ontology source: CCO 1.7.
https://github.com/CommonCoreOntology/CommonCoreOntologies/releases/tag/v1.7-2024-11-03"""@en ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ,
                                                                               "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "ClimOO Ontology - ClimOO-SDC2 module"@en ,
                                                                             "L'ontologia fondazionale della sostenibilità"@it ,
                                                                             "L'ontologie fondationnelle de la durabilité"@fr ,
                                                                             "Sustainability Core Ontology (SCO)"@en ,
                                                                             "BFO 2020" ;
                                            rdfs:comment """Currently, ClimOO-SDC2 focuses on the climate and climate change of the planet Earth. Nevertheless, it maintains a sufficiently flexible structure to accommodate and implement models concerning other planets.

According to relevant literature, the current representation leverages knowledge on climate and climate change, primarily referring to present and past climate trends, while climate change impacts are primarily addressed in terms of present and future effects."""@en ,
                                                         """The SDC Ontology provides a relevant model of climate and climate change, primarily with a focus on Sustainable Development Goals (Davarpanah et al., 2023). Despite its relevance, the SDC Onto model appears undermaintained and presents several shortcomings, including:
• Inconsistent hierarchy root.
• Absence of natural language definitions.
• Reusage of PATO representations that violate the BFO model, such as those concerning process properties, or that are inaccurate, such as those concerning increased and decreased dependent continuants.
• Misleadingness of certain classes.
• Inadequate axiomatization of certain classes.
For more details, see here (coming soon).

Thus, we forked SDC Onto to develop a novel version, named ClimOO-SDC2. ClimOO-SDC2 is the module of the ClimOO Ontology dedicated to climate change. ClimOO-SDC2 focuses on environmental features and related interconnections modeled in SDC Onto. ClimOO-SDC2 offers an active reference hub that addresses SDC Onto's shortcomings, while integrating the SDC Onto model into the ClimOO Ontology. ClimOO-SDC2 extends SCO, aligning the SDC Onto model with primary existing BFO-compliant sustainability ontologies. We intend ClimOO-SDC2 as an initial starting point to establish a unique BFO-compliant representation of climate and climate change. 

To construct ClimOO-SDC2, we proceed as follows (focus on OWL classes; we applied the same approach concerning the other OWL building blocks).
• If the class was not relevant, we did not import it.
• If the class was relevant and adequate, we directly imported it.
• If the class was relevant but inadequately axiomatized, we created a corresponding class that supports appropriate axioms but maintains the local identifier of the original SDC Onto class. We opted for this solution to offer a direct strategy of reference to the original version from which SDC2 has been forked. In the future, alternative, possibly more robust, strategies can be implemented. Exceptions: Given their centrality in the model, the following class has been supplied with ClimOO local identifiers and annotated towards original SDC Onto classes:
   • climate
   • climate change
   • (atmospheric) weather
   • climate system process
   • climate system component 
• If the class, despite axiomatization, was misleading, we did not import it, and we created adequate class(es) as needed. We supplied it with a ClimOO local identifier.
When revising classes, we complied with BFO and OBO-Foundry best practices.

All SDC2 building blocks support the following namespace to ensure appropriate identification and fairness: https://www.w3id.org/climoo/climoo-sdc2#

Bibliography
Davarpanah, A., Babaie, H., & Dhakal, N. (2023). Semantic modeling of climate change impacts on the implementation of the U.N. sustainable development goals related to poverty, hunger, water, and energy. Earth Sci. Inf., 16(1), 929–943."""@en ,
                                                         """This file contains ClimOO Ontology imports from the Sustainable Development and Climate ontology (SDC ontology) (generically dependent continuant hierarchy of BFO). It also contains some imports reused by SDC ontology from the Common Core Ontologies (CCO). Imports were manually collected and revised.

Ontology source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hbabaie1/Sustainable-Development-and-Climate-SDC-ontology/refs/heads/main/SDC_v1.owl"""@en ,
                                                         """This file contains ClimOO Ontology imports manually fletched from the Relation Ontology (RO).

Ontology source: https://github.com/oborel/obo-relations/releases/tag/v2025-12-17"""@en ,
                                                         "This file contains additional ClimOO Ontology imports from the Phenotype And Trait Ontology (PATO). These imports have been manually fletched from PATO."@en ,
                                                         """Three new releases of CCO, CCO 1.7, CCO 2.0, and CCO 2.1 have been made available between November 2024 and April 2026. CCO 2.0 provides a new IRI schema. SCO, ClimOO upper-level ontology, imports from a former release, CCO 1.5. Aiming to conform with SCO, ClimOO currently reuses CCO imports in compliance with SCO. As soon as updates are made available for those resources, ClimOO will align accordingly. 

https://github.com/CommonCoreOntology/CommonCoreOntologies/releases
https://w3id.org/sco/repo"""@en ,
                                                         "We currently imported all object properties we consider useful. We will revise RO imports as needed, possible excluding further object properties not needed for the Purposes of the ClimOO Ontology."@en ,
                                                         "The most recent version of this file will always be in the GitHub repository https://github.com/bfo-ontology/bfo-2020" ;
                                            rdfs:seeAlso """This file contains ClimOO Ontology imports from the Platform MaterialDigital Core Ontology (PMDco). Imports were manually collected and revised.
Ontology source: 
https://github.com/materialdigital/core-ontology/releases/tag/v3.0.0"""@en ,
                                                         "Ubbiali, G. A., Borghini, A., & Lange, M. C. (2024). Ontologies for Sustainability: Theoretical Challenges. https://doi.org/10.31219/osf.io/z8uqr" ,
                                                         "https://github.com/CommonCoreOntology/CommonCoreOntologies" ,
                                                         "https://github.com/hbabaie1/Sustainable-Development-and-Climate-SDC-ontology/tree/main" ,
                                                         "https://github.com/pato-ontology/pato/releases/tag/v2025-05-14" ,
                                                         "https://oborel.github.io/" ,
