###  http://www.ontologyrepository.com/CommonCoreOntologies/GainOfDependentContinuant
<http://www.ontologyrepository.com/CommonCoreOntologies/GainOfDependentContinuant> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                                   rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015> ;
                                                                                   <http://www.ontologyrepository.com/CommonCoreOntologies/definition> "A Change in which an Independent Continuant becomes the bearer or carrier of some Dependent Continuant."@en ;
                                                                                   <http://www.ontologyrepository.com/CommonCoreOntologies/is_curated_in_ontology> "http://www.ontologyrepository.com/CommonCoreOntologies/Mid/EventOntology"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                                                                   rdfs:comment """ClimOO Ontology comment:
We included loss/increase/decrease of dependent continuant classes as relevant for modelling purposes. However, we excluded the upper-level class change as not in compliance with BFO representation (Arp et al., 2015). We referred those aforementioned classes directly to the BFO process class as the immediate upper-level class. There are discussions going on concerning representing change under BFO. See for instance Ceusters & Ruttenberg (2025).
http://www.ontologyrepository.com/CommonCoreOntologies/Change 

Arp, R., Smith, B., & Spear, A. D. (2015). Building ontologies with Basic Formal Ontology. Massachusetts Institute of Technology.
Ceusters, W., & Ruttenberg, A. (2025). Towards Representing Change in the BFO. In T. Prince Sales, C. Masolo, & C. M. Keet (Eds.), Frontiers in Artificial Intelligence and Applications. IOS Press. https://doi.org/10.3233/FAIA250486"""@en ;
                                                                                   rdfs:label "Gain of Dependent Continuant"@en .


###  http://www.ontologyrepository.com/CommonCoreOntologies/GainOfDisposition
<http://www.ontologyrepository.com/CommonCoreOntologies/GainOfDisposition> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                           rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.ontologyrepository.com/CommonCoreOntologies/GainOfRealizableEntity> ,
                                                                                           [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                                             owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000057> ;
                                                                                             owl:someValuesFrom [ owl:intersectionOf ( <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004>
                                                                                                                                       [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                                                                                         owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000196> ;
                                                                                                                                         owl:someValuesFrom <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016>
                                                                                                                                       ]
                                                                                                                                     ) ;
                                                                                                                  rdf:type owl:Class
                                                                                                                ]
                                                                                           ] ;
                                                                           <http://www.ontologyrepository.com/CommonCoreOntologies/definition> "A Gain of Realizable Entity in which some Independent Continuant becomes the bearer of some Disposition."@en ;
                                                                           <http://www.ontologyrepository.com/CommonCoreOntologies/is_curated_in_ontology> "http://www.ontologyrepository.com/CommonCoreOntologies/Mid/EventOntology"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                                                           rdfs:comment "This class should be used to demarcate the start of the temporal interval (through the occurs_on property) that the Entity bears the Disposition."@en ;
                                                                           rdfs:label "Gain of Disposition"@en .


